#: 4749261f3edb4a75aa401c6f2e9cc592
msgid "[Bruco tutorial](../coupling/advanced_bruco.ipynb) — Bruco basics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:10015
#: 2aa59253b750455ea73abe0d14617e94
msgid ""
"[PCA/ICA tutorial](../fitting/advanced_decomposition.ipynb) — decomposition "
"basics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:20002
#: a1eebfb038dd4aab86cf27b603c48fbd
msgid "Setup"
msgstr "準備"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:40002
#: ffbfbd50a4b24e6f8d671e2582930605
msgid "1. Mock Data Generation"
msgstr "1. モックデータ生成"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:40004
#: 9f3f4bfc48db4dca9ca63c346ad9d3ed
msgid "We simulate a scenario where the DARM channel contains:"
msgstr "DARM チャンネルに以下が混入するシナリオをシミュレートします："

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:40005
#: a73f90cb215641198eaa636fac788d0c
msgid "Broadband Gaussian noise (the \"signal\" floor)"
msgstr "広帯域ガウスノイズ（バックグラウンド雑音フロア）"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:40006
#: 6be6aa0424444ab8b94c14681fe93145
msgid "A 116 Hz line noise leaking from environmental sensors"
msgstr "環境センサーから漏れた 116 Hz ラインノイズ"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:40008
#: 4d8a26dae703432f85462d6c5fbc5931
msgid ""
"Four PEM (Physical Environment Monitor) auxiliary channels each contain "
"varying amounts of the same 116 Hz line.  This mirrors the real O4b "
"commissioning case."
msgstr ""
"4 つの PEM（Physical Environment Monitor）補助チャンネルは、それぞれ異なる割合で同じ 116 Hz ラインを含みます。"
" これは O4b コミッショニングの実際のケースを模倣しています。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:70002
#: cef1967e74f049f0bdcf895620cc7c91
msgid "2. Bruco: Identify Correlated Auxiliary Channels"
msgstr "2. Bruco: 相関補助チャンネルの特定"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:70004
#: 295749949c684af995072aec021dc683
msgid ""
"`Bruco.compute()` scans all auxiliary channels and returns the top-*N* most "
"coherent channels at each frequency.  This is the **first stage** of the "
"pipeline: identify *which* sensors see the same noise as DARM."
msgstr ""
"`Bruco.compute()` は全補助チャンネルをスキャンし、各周波数ビンで上位 *N* 件の最相関チャンネルを返します。 これがパイプラインの "
"**第 1 ステージ** です：DARM と同じノイズを観測しているセンサーを特定します。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:70008
#: aaf8571db34f445d8382871623d90115
msgid ""
"**Common mistake**: feeding every available witness into ICA. Bruco is used "
"here as a physics filter so the decomposition focuses on channels that "
"plausibly share the 116 Hz contamination."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:110002
#: a26d05dfaa384b11ae046801e403b84f
msgid "3. ICA: Separate Noise Sources"
msgstr "3. ICA: ノイズ源の分離"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:110004
#: 32daa9be9419474d954fd2bc1c193c0b
msgid ""
"From the Bruco scan we know which channels are highly coherent with DARM "
"near 116 Hz. We now stack these channels into a `TimeSeriesMatrix` and apply"
" **ICA** to unmix the underlying independent sources."
msgstr ""
"Bruco スキャンから、DARM と 116 Hz 付近で高いコヒーレンスを持つチャンネルが分かりました。 次にこれらのチャンネルを "
"`TimeSeriesMatrix` に積み上げ、**ICA** を適用して 独立したノイズ源を分離します。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:110008
#: 21bf22a72d7d4cddbac4d0ffeb32672d
msgid "The ICA model gives us a *mixing matrix* **A** such that:"
msgstr "ICA モデルは混合行列 **A** を求めます："

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:110012
#: 0fcfe458fc4b4f9f841a81d0a13d540b
msgid "We can then subtract the noise-source contributions from DARM."
msgstr "この行列を使って DARM からノイズ成分の寄与を差し引けます。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:110014
#: 8d4b9901aa7d45ea8c69411e8cd807f8
msgid ""
"**Failure mode to watch for**: ICA components are not automatically ordered "
"by physical importance, and the sign / scale of each component is arbitrary."
" Always inspect spectra and channel loadings before deciding which component"
" represents the line you want to subtract."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:120002
#: 60b65c259d354f71957e00a8c3b16f98
msgid ""
"**Note — ICA convergence**: FastICA may not converge within the default "
"number of iterations on some datasets. If a `ConvergenceWarning` appears, "
"consider increasing `max_iter` or `tol` in the ICA parameters. Results may "
"still be usable even without full convergence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:120004
#: f991c1cd42424c08ac0f7dc6d316a921
msgid ""
"A second common failure mode is rank deficiency: if you feed nearly "
"identical witnesses into ICA, the decomposition becomes unstable and the "
"subtraction weights are hard to trust. Prefer a small set of informative but"
" not perfectly redundant channels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:150002
#: 837850ffad7341f5852b75456d90a89c
msgid "4. Noise Subtraction and ASD Comparison"
msgstr "4. ノイズ差し引きと ASD 比較"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:150004
#: 42d6ab9f0d094411a8ce553acdd62926
msgid ""
"Identify which ICA components contain the 116 Hz line (by inspecting the "
"ASD), then subtract their contribution from DARM using the mixing matrix."
msgstr "116 Hz ラインを含む ICA 成分を特定し（ASD を確認して選択）、 混合行列を使って DARM からその寄与を差し引きます。"

#: ../../how-to/case-studies/case_bruco_ica_denoising.ipynb:150011
#: 3fa9232aafac458bb229018a1bdf4952
msgid ""
"**Common mistake**: subtracting every ICA component that looks non-Gaussian."
" Only subtract components whose spectral content and witness loadings match "
"the targeted coupling mechanism; otherwise you risk removing unrelated "
"detector structure along with the line."
msgstr ""

